## **Performance Optimization**

### **Code Splitting**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Dynamic imports for large components
import dynamic from "next/dynamic";

const ShipmentChart = dynamic(() => import("@/components/features/ShipmentChart"), {
  loading: () => <div className="animate-pulse h-64 bg-gray-200 rounded" />,
  ssr: false,
});

// ✅ CORRECT: Lazy loading with React.lazy
const HeavyModal = lazy(() => import("@/components/modals/HeavyModal"));
```

### **Memoization**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Memoize expensive components
const ShipmentList = memo(({ shipments, onSelect }: ShipmentListProps) => {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-2">
      {shipments.map((shipment) => (
        <ShipmentCard key={shipment.id} shipment={shipment} onSelect={onSelect} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
});

// ✅ CORRECT: Memoize expensive calculations
const shipmentStats = useMemo(() => {
  return {
    total: shipments.length,
    delivered: shipments.filter(s => s.status === "delivered").length,
    pending: shipments.filter(s => s.status === "in-transit").length,
  };
}, [shipments]);
```

## **Standards Checklist**

### **MANDATORY: Every Component Must Have**

- [ ] TypeScript interface for props
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] Loading states
- [ ] Responsive design (mobile-first)
- [ ] Accessibility attributes (ARIA labels)
- [ ] Consistent styling with Tailwind utilities

### **NEVER DO**

- ❌ Use `any` type without good reason
- ❌ Inline styles instead of Tailwind classes
- ❌ Hardcode API URLs (use environment variables)
- ❌ Skip error boundaries for complex components
- ❌ Ignore accessibility requirements

### **ALWAYS DO**

- ✅ Use TypeScript for all components
- ✅ Implement proper loading and error states
- ✅ Follow component hierarchy (ui → forms → features)
- ✅ Use Zustand for global state management
- ✅ Implement responsive design patterns
- ✅ Add proper ARIA labels for accessibility